+# Cancellation
+
+For whoever changes cancellation eligibility or answers a member who can no longer cancel a pantry order in the
+app. Cancellation closes when packing starts, two hours before pickup. Late cancellations left packed bags of fresh
+food on the shelf; a banner asking members to cancel earlier had been in place since summer, but 25 bags of fresh
+food were thrown away in early October.
+
+## Cutoff
+
+A member can cancel only before the point two hours before their pickup slot starts. At that point and afterwards,
+the app refuses cancellation. For a 17:00 pickup, cancellation is allowed before 15:00 and refused at 15:00.
+The [eligibility check](../../larder/cancellation.py) defines the boundary.
+
+The packing shift starts two hours before each slot. Cancellations before packing cost the pantry nothing;
+cancellations after packing starts waste a packed bag. The cutoff follows that shift.
+
+## After the cutoff
+
+A member who cannot come calls the pantry, and the volunteers decide what to do. The refusal message must include
+the pantry's phone number so the member can reach them.
+
+## Known limits
+
+The repository contains the eligibility check but no refusal message or pantry phone number. When integrating the
+check into a member-facing flow, supply the pantry's actual phone number with the refusal so members can use the
+phone fallback.
